  "id": "contrast-effect",
  "term": "contrast effect",
  "definition": "In historical psychology, contrast effect refers to the way one feeling or perception is altered by another occurring at the same time or just before or after it. The term was used especially for affective changes, such as shifts between hope and fear or joy and sorrow, and also for visual effects seen between the two eyes.",
